  "text_md": "## SCE in Nephrology Blueprint\n\nout in the syllabus of the curriculum. The composition of the paper is as follows: **Topic** Glomerulonephritis, tubulointerstitial nephritis (incl. vasculitis, anti-GBM disease, SLE) Acute kidney injury, acute renal replacement therapy, disorders of fluid, electrolytes and acid base Chronic kidney disease, haematuria, proteinuria Renal bone disease, renal anaemia Cardiovascular disease, hypertension, renovascular disease and diabetes Urological presentations including renal stone disease, urinary tract infection and obstruction Inherited and rarer diseases Peritoneal dialysis Haemodialysis Renal transplantation Other^ **Total**\n\n## MRCP(UK) Central Office\n\n11 St Andrews Place Regent’s Park London NW1 4LE Tel: +44 (0)20 3075 1515 **www.mrcpuk.org**\n\n## Number of questions*\n\n26 24 12 20\n\n14 14 8 14 14 24 **200**\n\nCandidates are tested on a wide range of common and important disorders as set\n\nThe questions in each category are distributed across both papers\n\n|*This should be taken as an indication of the likely number of questions – the actual number may vary.||\n|---|---|\n|^ ‘Other’ includes the following topics:||\n|prescribing|cal procedures|\n|s in pregnancy||\n|Infection in the renal patient|Adult-paediatric interface|\n|Active supportive (non-dialysis) care|End-of-life care MP|\n|trition||\n",
